<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Analysis>
    <Title>KB5022842 on Win 2022</Title>
    <Description>Only relevant for Win2022.
Looks up installed hotfix KB5022842 via wmis and checks registry to see check state of secure boot.

Confirmed to work if both values are True.
It will result in the VM getting tripped up next boot if running on vmware.
Might happen to all Hypervisors, but none in our environment.

Can be easily modified to look for whatever specific KB you are trying to locate.
</Description>
    <Relevance>( (name of it as lowercase = &quot;Win2022&quot; as lowercase ) of operating system)</Relevance>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Mon, 20 Feb 2023 12:50:53 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <Property ID="1" Name="KB installed" EvaluationPeriod="PT5M">(exists (string values of properties &quot;HotFixID&quot; of it) whose (it = &quot;KB5022842&quot;) of select objects &quot;HotFixID from Win32_QuickFixEngineering&quot; of wmis) as string</Property>
    <Property ID="3" Name="Secure Boot Enabled ">exists it whose(1 = it as integer) of unique values of (it as string) of values &quot;UEFISecureBootEnabled&quot; of keys &quot;HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\SecureBoot\State&quot; of (x64 registries; x32 registries)</Property>
  </Analysis>
</BES>
